<title>GERMANY: Viag dismisses talk of telecoms start-up losses.</title>
<headline>Viag dismisses talk of telecoms start-up losses.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>German diversified utility group Viag AG on Friday dismissed market speculation that higher telecommunications start-up costs would affect its earnings.</p>
<p>The group said that the fall in its share price over the day was normal market fluctuation.</p>
<p>Viag shares were down 8.50 marks at 766 marks in late bourse trade, off a low of 753 marks.</p>
</text>
